WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.067
-Martin Short, welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.767
-James.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:07.033
James Thomas Fallon.
-Yes.

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:09.901
-My God, your name screams out
diversity.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.067
It really does.

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:13.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:16.501
I'm so excited to be here
tonight.

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:18.667
Although, it could be
the Vicodin and Xanax talking,

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:20.300
but I don't think so.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:24.801
In fact, it's hard for me to
express how excited I am to be

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:27.400
here tonight because
the Botox is fresh.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.968
-Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.834
Can barely tell.
You can barely see anything.

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:33.133
-You know, I haven't seen you

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:36.467
since the big Saudi golf
tournament.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:40.000
Who knew that you and the crown
prince were such buddies?

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.868
The giggling and the giggling,

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.634
and he's knitting
and you're holding the wool.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:46.501
It's so beautiful.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:49.400
In fact, tell everyone what you
were telling me about why

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.601
the Proud Boys is so much more
than a club.

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:53.167
What did you mean by that?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:54.667
What does that mean?

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.701
What does that mean?

00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:00.534
No, no, Jimmy --
Here's the thing about Jimmy.

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:03.300
We do hang out because we're not
just fake show-business friends.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.133
We're fake friends in real life.
-That's right.

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:06.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:08.434
We really are. That is correct.

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.267
How is your summer going,
though?

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:12.400
-Well, it's so beautiful.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.033
I've been up -- I've been up
with the loons at my cottage.

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:20.267
And do I regret my "Kim and Pete
Forever" tattoo? Sure.

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:23.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.501
Absolutely.
-You can fix it.

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:28.300
-Regrets, I've had a few.
-Do I? Yes, I do.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.000
-Oh, and how about this?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.567
You know, I was at Mar-a-Lago
during the big FBI raid.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:36.834
-Wait, what?
-Oh, I'm gonna lie.

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:38.968
No, I'm a member there.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:41.567
-I did not know you're a member
of Mar-a-Lago.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:45.234
-I don't like Trump's politics,
but I love his omelet station.

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:47.000
[ Laughter ]
-That makes sense.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.601
-It's so beautiful.

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:50.934
And it's so great because you
can just -- if you're a member,

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:52.934
you can just read as many
classified documents

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:54.667
as you want.
They're all over the place.

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:55.901
-They're just scattered
everywhere.

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:59.667
I didn't even know
you knew the Trumps.

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:00.934
-Oh, I know the Trumps.

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:03.834
I used to babysit the kids,
for God's sake.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:07.334
Eric and Don Jr., we would play
Monopoly, but their version is

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:09.534
the winner is the first person
to yell bankruptcy.

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:15.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.534
-That's another fun way
to play it.

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:19.234
-Someone's been doing
some writin'.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:22.267
-How's our pal, Steve Martin,
doing?

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:23.667
That's what I'm talking about.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.400
-You know, Steve --
Well, first of all,

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.067
he's the most talented guy
in the world, you know.

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:35.067
I mean, he -- he does magic.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:37.367
He juggles. He plays the banjo.

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:39.667
And yet somehow, he's famous.
I don't know how.

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:41.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:44.934
We're a team now. We're like
Florida and a lower-back tattoo.

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:47.400
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.133
I want to congratulate you
on this tour, by the way,

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:52.133
okay, because yeah, this is a --

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:54.133
I mean, what have you learned,
by the way --

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:56.367
what have you learned touring
with Steve Martin?

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:59.133
-Well...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:03.133
I've learned that he will pay
top dollar for clean urine.

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:04.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:06.267
-You got to pass those tests.
You got to pass the test.

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:09.100
-I've learned from him
that you don't need to

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.734
have a pool to have a pool boy.

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:13.601
-Hello!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:16.434
-No, but he is really amazing.
He's such a unique --

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:19.367
You know, he butt-dialed me
the other day, which is kind of

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:21.567
remarkable 'cause he still has
a rotary phone so...

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.033
[ Laughter ]
-That's very hard to do.

00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:25.501
-Oh, not for Steve.

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:27.934
Not when you have that talent.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:30.667
-I want to congratulate
you and Steve.

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:33.267
You're both Emmy-nominated for
"Only Murders in the Building."

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:36.033
-Yes. 17.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:40.868
-The show got a whopping
17 Emmy nominations.

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:41.901
That is amazing.

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:43.267
-And I'm just letting
you know --

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:45.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you. Thank you.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:49.300
-You are fantastic.
-And I'm just letting you know,

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:51.367
I'm making it red-carpet
official

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:54.067
with Liz Cheney when I go there.

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.834
-You heard it here first.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.300
-But -- No, no, no.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.868
Here's the thing. The show --

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:01.000
First of all, the finale is
on next Tuesday, you know?

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.734
-That's right.
-Episode 10.

00:04:02.734 --> 00:04:04.734
Who did it?
-I'm excited.

00:04:04.734 --> 00:04:06.334
-You know, Steve and I are
nominated.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:10.467
And, you know, if I can't win,
I hope he wins.

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:12.501
But I can win,
so screw him, you know?

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:14.267
-No, no, no, that's not
what you want.

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:17.200
No, but you are nominated for
the exact same category.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.367
-I know.
-So, yeah, you have to --

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:22.200
You either win or if you lose --

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.501
-If I lose, I'm going to send
Will Smith up to slap him.

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:27.300
-No, no, no.
-Why not?

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.901
-He won't be there.
He won't be there for the Emmys.

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:31.400
-Here's the thing.
Here's what's amazing.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.000
Here's what's amazing.
If someone had told me

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.834
20 years ago that I would be on

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:39.167
"The Tonight Show
with Jimmy Fallon"

00:04:39.167 --> 00:04:41.300
with all these Emmy nominations,

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.767
I would have said,
"Jimmy Fallon?"

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:45.667
[ Laughter and applause ]
-That's interesting.

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:48.467
I never thought of it that way.
-Never thought of it that way.

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.033
-"Only Murders in the Building."

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.067
It's the best acting I can do
to not laugh at everything.

00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:56.701
You were phenomenal.

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:58.334
I want to just say this
for real.

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:00.167
No bits, nothing,
I'm not doing anything.

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:02.667
I just want to say,
in this show, I've loved you,

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:03.968
I love all your work.

00:05:03.968 --> 00:05:06.467
But this is something that
no one else can do.

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:09.167
You do comedy and you do drama

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:11.734
and you make me cry
and you make me laugh.

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.968
You were amazing in the show.

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:16.200
And congratulations.
-Thank you very much.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you!

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:20.133
-Martin Short,
"Only Murders in the Building."

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:23.467
Really, I can't even tell you --
I can't even tell you.

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:25.834
-That is very lovely.
-I want to show a clip.

00:05:25.834 --> 00:05:27.234
Do you want to set up this clip?

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:31.167
-Oh, this clip is -- In the
show, I find out that my son

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:35.100
might not be my DNA son,
and I'm panicked by it.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:38.334
So I go and get a DNA test,
and this is me anxiously,

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:40.901
filled with anxiety,
waiting to do the test.

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:42.300
-Here we go.
Here's Martin Short in

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.534
"Only Murders in the Building."
Take a look at this.

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:47.067
-So apparently, my son is Greek,

00:05:47.067 --> 00:05:50.234
which means that I must be
Greek, not Irish.

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:52.667
Surprise.

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:55.334
But of course, it makes,
you know, complete sense

00:05:55.334 --> 00:05:58.534
when you think about the Greeks,
founders of Western theater.

00:05:58.534 --> 00:06:01.133
Father of the public bathhouse.

00:06:01.133 --> 00:06:02.767
Sound like anyone you just met?

00:06:02.767 --> 00:06:04.300
[ Laughs ]

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:11.667
-We tell ourselves it can't
possibly be true.

00:06:11.667 --> 00:06:14.067
-Am I nervous that my son
isn't my son?

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:15.534
Not at all.

00:06:15.534 --> 00:06:18.033
In fact, the only thing I am
nervous about is producing

00:06:18.033 --> 00:06:19.934
enough spit for this test
because my mouth

00:06:19.934 --> 00:06:21.834
is so dry right now.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.400
Anyone else have a dry mouth?

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:27.968 --> 00:06:30.467
-Martin Short, everybody!

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:33.601
The season two finale of
"Only Murders in the Building"

00:06:33.601 --> 00:06:35.801
airs Tuesday on Hulu.

